│ patch_description        │ Uses an ecology-normalized mutation budget instead of fixed sparse regimes. The scheduler │
│                          │ first estimates whether mutation is worth spending from population stress, recovery       │
│                          │ capacity, parent quality, and genome compactness, then allocates that limited budget      │
│                          │ through trusted operator evidence relative to clone. Weak or untrusted evidence is shrunk │
│                          │ toward conservative priors, so exploratory/structural operators only rise when both       │
│                          │ ecology and operator evidence support them. This keeps an ecology-conditioned non-clone   │
│                          │ mechanism while reducing founder-specific over-triggering.                                │
