│ patch_description        │ This edit makes mutation pressure depend more on ecology-normalized distress and          │
│                          │ cross-operator trust, instead of subtracting clone trust directly. The current            │
│                          │ relative-trust term appears to have made the policy more clone-heavy and reduced both     │
│                          │ sham and shock deltas. The replacement adds a bounded injury-like rescue gate from intake │
│                          │ deficit, decline/death pressure, low growth, and birth scarcity, then uses                │
│                          │ evidence-weighted non-clone advantage only when operators have real evidence. It also     │
│                          │ applies a calm/growth penalty to poorly evidenced operators so exploratory, structural,   │
│                          │ and mixed mutations do not over-trigger on sealed founders. The mechanism remains         │
│                          │ ecology-conditioned and non-constant, with small but genuine high-pressure scout boosts.  │
